built.best:
gta_xv_conservative is the best overall; the medoid-linkage version is about equal. Compared with the baseline (ids 61/59, top10 0.704/0.72, events 12.7/13.0, team_imp 0.025/0.018, 5v5 0.46/0.51), it gives:
- ids 28/29, with 10 IDs over half the window in both halves;
- top10 0.836/0.873;
- events 5.0/6.7 per min, about half the baseline;
- team_imp 0.013/0.010, about half the baseline;
- 5v5 0.53/0.51;
- appearance breaks 0/1 per min, 0 double-used boxes, box_coverage 0.97.

The numbers hold across both halves.

Where it is worse:
- speed_jumps is 22.7/26.7 per min against the baseline's 10/20. This is after smoothing; without smoothing it is about 34 (first half). The jumps come from single-view jitter of the far-side foot points and Hermite fills between noisy end velocities. Wrong links are only a part.
- 2.5% of good boxes are dropped (unattached crossing debris).

gta_fused35 is the runner-up. It has the lowest jumps and teleports in the first half (19.7, 17.7) but higher team_imp (0.019) and appearance breaks (1.7-2.7 per min), and lower 5v5 (0.40/0.43). Fusing per frame mixes identities that the per-camera route keeps apart.

boosttrack has the best second-half 5v5 (0.595) but 45-58 speed jumps per min. hybridsort is unusable here: the cam1 and cam2 copies of a player stay as duplicates (mean_Y 5.7-6.0, over5 0.8-0.9, dup 18-19).

The swap score never flagged anything, but only 0-8 crossings are scored per half, so it is not evidence either way.
